(7751153, 1279811, 273619, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Pangurban:</b></div><hr/><i> A great catch but in this challenge I am looking for a distinct subject for a portrait; this strikes me more as a ''scene'' than a portrait. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I appreciate your opinion but my understanding of a portrait is very similar to this definition: "Portrait photography is best defined as a genre of photography that involves capturing the identity, personality, facial expression, soul, emotions, essence, and the overall inherent character of a subject within a photograph." I think there is a lot of misconception when it comes to portraits as they don''t need to be one subject or a headshot. Just my own opinion.</td>', 'Originally posted by Pangurban: A great catch but in this challenge I am looking for a distinct subject for a portrait; this strikes me more as a ''scene'' than a portrait.   I appreciate your opinion but my understanding of a portrait is very similar to this definition: "Portrait photography is best defined as a genre of photography that involves capturing the identity, personality, facial expression, soul, emotions, essence, and the overall inherent character of a subject within a photograph." I think there is a lot of misconception when it comes to portraits as they don''t need to be one subject or a headshot. Just my own opinion.', '2023-06-21 01:15:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7751155, 1279759, 273854, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NikonJeb:</b></div><hr/><i> Well..... People squawk if you leave a low vote without an explanation.<br/> <br/>I am putting in the caveat that this is a combination of my opinion and impression(s).<br/> <br/>I''m giving you a 3.<br/> <br/>From a straight up presentation with conventional editing, it''s not super sharp. I''d like to have a feel for what I am supposed to see here. I don''t know what the intended focal point is. Assuming that it''s the nest, it''s dead center which is a tough composition to fly.<br/> <br/>I mentioned the sharpness, and the branches in the top right corner are beyond distracting, in my perspective. There''s another single, errant branch in the lower right corner. Also in that lower right corner there''s another peculiar element that is odd.<br/> <br/>I honestly cannot conjure up anything from this offering that says "Portrait" to me.<br/> <br/>Anyhow for me </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thankyou!! After it opened for voting I realised I had completely missed the ''Portrait'' part to the competition! Oh well.... lesson learned!</td>', 'Originally posted by NikonJeb: Well..... People squawk if you leave a low vote without an explanation. I am putting in the caveat that this is a combination of my opinion and impression(s). I''m giving you a 3. From a straight up presentation with conventional editing, it''s not super sharp. I''d like to have a feel for what I am supposed to see here. I don''t know what the intended focal point is. Assuming that it''s the nest, it''s dead center which is a tough composition to fly. I mentioned the sharpness, and the branches in the top right corner are beyond distracting, in my perspective. There''s another single, errant branch in the lower right corner. Also in that lower right corner there''s another peculiar element that is odd. I honestly cannot conjure up anything from this offering that says "Portrait" to me. Anyhow for me   Thankyou!! After it opened for voting I realised I had completely missed the ''Portrait'' part to the competition! Oh well.... lesson learned!', '2023-06-21 01:20:27.000000', NULL, 0),
