(7751179, 1280802, 83313, '<td valign="top">I see neither of us were as original with that title as we thought we were being, and we both got creamed in voting. Not unexpected.<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1280321" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3604/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1280321.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3604/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1280321.jpg'', strrpos(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3604/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1280321.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a> <br/> <br/>The bug you mentioned in the date acceptance is a known issue. You did the appropriate thing. If an image gets requested for a validation, the date encoded in the original capture is what matters.</td>', 'I see neither of us were as original with that title as we thought we were being, and we both got creamed in voting. Not unexpected.  The bug you mentioned in the date acceptance is a known issue. You did the appropriate thing. If an image gets requested for a validation, the date encoded in the original capture is what matters.', '2023-06-21 01:37:35.000000', NULL, 0),
